  "methods": ["compound angle formula", "rewriting sin^2 in terms of cos"],
  "statement": "Prove that $\\sin 3\\theta=3\\sin\\theta-4\\sin^{3}\\theta$.",
  "solution": "Write $\\sin3\\theta=\\sin(2\\theta+\\theta)$:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sin3\\theta&=\\sin2\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\cos2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\n&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos^{2}\\theta+(1-2\\sin^{2}\\theta)\\sin\\theta\\\\\n&=2\\sin\\theta(1-\\sin^{2}\\theta)+\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^{3}\\theta\\\\\n&=2\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^{3}\\theta+\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^{3}\\theta\\\\\n&=3\\sin\\theta-4\\sin^{3}\\theta.\n\\end{align*}",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Write sin 3θ = sin(2θ+θ).",
    "Use the double-angle formulas for sin and cos.",
    "Replace cos^2θ by 1 - sin^2θ."
  ]
}
